MemoryError: BindCraft 2 ran out of device memory in the Evoformer backward at 640 tokens.
  complex   627 residues, padded to 640 tokens (tt-bio buckets the token axis to 32)
  asked for 5.2 MB in one DRAM buffer (0.4 MB in each of 12 banks)
  free      109.4 MB of 12.885 GB, largest contiguous block 0.2 MB
This is fragmentation, not a full card: 109.4 MB is free, which would cover the 5.2 MB request if it were in one piece, but the largest contiguous block in a bank is 0.2 MB against the 0.4 MB that bank needs.
What to do: run a smaller complex. The token axis is the complex BindCraft 2 built, padded to a multiple of 32 -- it is LARGER than target residues + binder length, so size the job off the 627 above and not off that sum. 19 residues off the binder takes this fold to 608 tokens. The largest axis measured to complete a gradient round on one p150a is 576 tokens. Trimming the target to the domain you are binding is the other lever and usually the bigger one.
The allocator's own refusal follows.
